{
  "info": {
    "name": "OpenG2P Aggregation Layer (Beneficiary-360)",
    "description": "The consent-gated Beneficiary-360 fetch on the Aggregation Layer (`agg_url`, default http://localhost:8110).\n\n## The flow\n\nThe subject's consent comes first, outside this service:\n\n1. the partner raises a consent request in the Consent Manager (`POST /consent/v1/consent-requests`); the CM sends the subject a one-time code;\n2. the partner gets the code from the subject and confirms it with the CM; the CM records the consent;\n3. the partner calls this service with a consent object it signed (`authorize.consent_jws`):\n   - `POST /dci/registry/sync/search` (default): `200`, the body is the signed DCI on-search whose `reg_records[0]` is the Beneficiary-360 response;\n   - `POST /dci/registry/async/search`: `202` ack; the same on-search is POSTed to `header.sender_uri` as soon as the registries have answered (one attempt, no retry).\n\nNo consent from the subject: `403 no_subject_consent`.\n\n## Before you start\n\n```bash\npython postman/agg-prep.py   # gives the subject an active consent, signs the consent object, writes the local environment\n```\n\n`agg-prep.py` does steps 1-2 for you (directly on the CM, as the subject). Import `OpenG2P-Aggregator.local.postman_environment.json` (generated, gitignored), select it, then run the folders in order. `python postman/agg-prep.py --no-grant` leaves the subject without a consent: the searches then answer `403 no_subject_consent`.\n\n## The consent object\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| expires | 300s (`replay_freshness_window_sec`) |\n| answered once | the CM records its first permit; a later search for other registries is `409 consent_object_reused` |\n\nRe-run `agg-prep.py` (and re-import the environment) if a search comes back `replay` or `consent_object_reused`.\n\n## Why Postman cannot do all of it\n\nA consent object is an ES256 compact JWS and Postman's sandbox has no ECDSA, so `agg-prep.py` signs it outside and hands it over as `{{consent_jws}}`. Everything else is plain HTTP.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "agg_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8110"
    },
    {
      "key": "keycloak_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "callback_receiver",
      "value": "http://localhost:9099"
    },
    {
      "key": "bene360_context",
      "value": "https://schemas.openg2p.org/beneficiary360/v1/context.jsonld"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 Health & discovery",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Service is up",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/ping",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ping"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('up', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Registry catalog",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/aggregation/v1/registries",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "aggregation",
                "v1",
                "registries"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every registry, its scopes (`scopeId` is what a partner consents to), where each block lands in the Beneficiary-360 response and which fields may leave the service. Open by design: no URL, binding or secret.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('catalog returned', () => pm.expect(j.registries).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "(j.registries || []).forEach(r => console.log(r.registryCode + ': ' +",
                  "  r.scopes.map(s => s.scopeId).join(', ')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 Partner - sync search (default)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Beneficiary-360 search (sync)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/dci/registry/sync/search",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "dci",
                "registry",
                "sync",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A DCI search envelope whose `search_criteria.query` is a Beneficiary-360 request; the consent object goes in `authorize.consent_jws`. The answer is the HTTP response: a signed DCI on-search whose `message.search_response[0].data.reg_records[0]` is the Beneficiary-360 response. `header.sender_uri` is not needed here. Without a subject consent: `403 no_subject_consent`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"header\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"message_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"message_ts\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"action\": \"search\",\n    \"sender_id\": \"{{partner_audience}}\",\n    \"receiver_id\": \"aggregation-layer\",\n    \"sender_uri\": \"{{callback_url}}\",\n    \"total_count\": 1,\n    \"is_msg_encrypted\": false\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"txn-{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"search_request\": [\n      {\n        \"reference_id\": \"ref-{{$timestamp}}\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n        \"search_criteria\": {\n          \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n          \"query_type\": \"beneficiary360\",\n          \"query\": {\n            \"@context\": \"{{bene360_context}}\",\n            \"foundationalId\": \"{{foundational_id}}\",\n            \"timeframe\": \"Timeframe-Medium\",\n            \"sections\": [\n              \"REGISTRIES\"\n            ],\n            \"correlationId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}\"\n          },\n          \"purpose\": {\n            \"code\": \"loan_origination\"\n          },\n          \"authorize\": {\n            \"consent_jws\": \"{{consent_jws}}\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('answered (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const res = ((j.message || {}).search_response || [{}])[0];",
                  "const rec = ((res.data || {}).reg_records || [])[0] || {};",
                  "pm.test('a signed DCI on-search', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.header.action).to.eql('on-search');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.signature).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('reg_records[0] is a Beneficiary-360 response', () => pm.expect(rec['@type']).to.eql('Beneficiary360Response'));",
                  "const target = pm.environment.name ? pm.environment : pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "if (j.message && j.message.correlation_id) { target.set('correlation_id', j.message.correlation_id); }",
                  "console.log('status      : ' + j.header.status);",
                  "console.log('registries  : ' + (rec.registries || []).map(r => r.registryCode).join(', '));",
                  "console.log('warnings    : ' + JSON.stringify((rec.meta || {}).warnings || []));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 Partner - async search and callback",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Beneficiary-360 search (async)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/dci/registry/async/search",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "dci",
                "registry",
                "async",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The same envelope on the async route. `header.sender_uri` is the callback. Answered `202` with an ack once every check (callback URL, query, consent) has passed; the signed on-search is POSTed to `sender_uri` as soon as the registries have answered. One attempt, no retry, not kept across a restart. Right before the callback the CM is asked again whether the consent is still active: if not, the callback is a rejected on-search (`consent_withdrawn`, or `consent_check_failed` when the CM cannot answer) without data.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"header\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"message_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"message_ts\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"action\": \"search\",\n    \"sender_id\": \"{{partner_audience}}\",\n    \"receiver_id\": \"aggregation-layer\",\n    \"sender_uri\": \"{{callback_url}}\",\n    \"total_count\": 1,\n    \"is_msg_encrypted\": false\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"txn-{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"search_request\": [\n      {\n        \"reference_id\": \"ref-{{$timestamp}}\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n        \"search_criteria\": {\n          \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n          \"query_type\": \"beneficiary360\",\n          \"query\": {\n            \"@context\": \"{{bene360_context}}\",\n            \"foundationalId\": \"{{foundational_id}}\",\n            \"timeframe\": \"Timeframe-Medium\",\n            \"sections\": [\n              \"REGISTRIES\"\n            ],\n            \"correlationId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}\"\n          },\n          \"purpose\": {\n            \"code\": \"loan_origination\"\n          },\n          \"authorize\": {\n            \"consent_jws\": \"{{consent_jws}}\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted (202)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('ack fields', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('pdng');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.correlation_id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.accepted_scopes).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(j.registries).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(j.callback_url).to.eql(pm.variables.get('callback_url'));",
                  "});",
                  "const target = pm.environment.name ? pm.environment : pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "if (j.correlation_id) { target.set('correlation_id', j.correlation_id); }",
                  "console.log('correlation : ' + j.correlation_id);",
                  "console.log('registries  : ' + (j.registries || []).join(', '));",
                  "console.log('scopes      : ' + (j.accepted_scopes || []).length);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Last on-search received (dev receiver)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{callback_receiver}}/last",
              "host": [
                "{{callback_receiver}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "last"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`postman/callback_receiver.py` (`agg-callback` in docker-compose). The pre-request script waits a few seconds for the registries to answer.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// the async answer is sent as soon as the registries have answered",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 3000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const body = j.body || j;",
                  "const msg = body.message || {};",
                  "const rec = (((msg.search_response || [{}])[0]).data || {}).reg_records || [];",
                  "pm.test('the on-search of the async search', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect((body.header || {}).action).to.eql('on-search');",
                  "  pm.expect(msg.correlation_id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('correlation_id'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('a Beneficiary-360 response', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect((rec[0] || {})['@type']).to.eql('Beneficiary360Response'));",
                  "console.log(JSON.stringify(rec[0], null, 2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 Guard rails",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Another beneficiary than the consent subject - 403",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/dci/registry/sync/search",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "dci",
                "registry",
                "sync",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`foundationalId` must be the consent object's subject: a consent for one person never fetches another.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"header\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"message_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"message_ts\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"action\": \"search\",\n    \"sender_id\": \"{{partner_audience}}\",\n    \"receiver_id\": \"aggregation-layer\",\n    \"sender_uri\": \"{{callback_url}}\",\n    \"total_count\": 1,\n    \"is_msg_encrypted\": false\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"txn-{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"search_request\": [\n      {\n        \"reference_id\": \"ref-{{$timestamp}}\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n        \"search_criteria\": {\n          \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n          \"query_type\": \"beneficiary360\",\n          \"query\": {\n            \"@context\": \"{{bene360_context}}\",\n            \"foundationalId\": \"someone-else\",\n            \"timeframe\": \"Timeframe-Medium\",\n            \"sections\": [\n              \"REGISTRIES\"\n            ],\n            \"correlationId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}\"\n          },\n          \"purpose\": {\n            \"code\": \"loan_origination\"\n          },\n          \"authorize\": {\n            \"consent_jws\": \"{{consent_jws}}\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 subject_mismatch', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('subject_mismatch');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Property bene-360 does not define - 400",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agg_url}}/dci/registry/sync/search",
              "host": [
                "{{agg_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "dci",
                "registry",
                "sync",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The query must validate against the published request.schema.json, which forbids extra properties.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"header\": {\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"message_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"message_ts\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"action\": \"search\",\n    \"sender_id\": \"{{partner_audience}}\",\n    \"receiver_id\": \"aggregation-layer\",\n    \"sender_uri\": \"{{callback_url}}\",\n    \"total_count\": 1,\n    \"is_msg_encrypted\": false\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"txn-{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"search_request\": [\n      {\n        \"reference_id\": \"ref-{{$timestamp}}\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n        \"search_criteria\": {\n          \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n          \"query_type\": \"beneficiary360\",\n          \"query\": {\n            \"@context\": \"{{bene360_context}}\",\n            \"foundationalId\": \"{{foundational_id}}\",\n            \"timeframe\": \"Timeframe-Medium\",\n            \"sections\": [\n              \"REGISTRIES\"\n            ],\n            \"correlationId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}\",\n            \"fields\": [\n              \"anything\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"purpose\": {\n            \"code\": \"loan_origination\"\n          },\n          \"authorize\": {\n            \"consent_jws\": \"{{consent_jws}}\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
